Why: on 6.12 the kernel ring is 128 KiB (GKI CONFIG_LOG_BUF_SHIFT=17, no log_buf_len on the command line);
5.4 has 1 MiB (CONFIG_LOG_BUF_SHIFT=20). The sec_battery monitor cycle (10 s while a charger/USB is present)
makes sm5714-charger print its register map TWICE per cycle (health read "please keep this log message" +
POWER_SUPPLY_EXT_PROP_MONITOR_WORK): 10 lines, ~1.45 KiB per cycle = 64 lines / 9.2 KiB per minute, the same
rate as 5.4 (68 lines / 9.8 KiB per minute in logs/selftest/PHONE1-20261122-172724/kmsg.txt). The code is
identical to 5.4; only the small ring makes it hurt (the whole ring holds ~1 minute of a One UI boot).

FIRST CHOICE (no driver change): a larger ring, as 5.4 has: build with DIAG_BOOTARGS="log_buf_len=1M" (or 4M for
a night of pm_debug_messages); DIAG_BOOTARGS already reaches the DT bootargs (rb99m ran log_buf_len=8M on a
real boot). This patch is the second, optional step.

What it does: chg_print_regmap() prints only when one of the 49 registers changed since the last print, or on
every 30th call (a heartbeat: every ~2.5 min at the 10 s cycle with two calls per cycle), and says how many
unchanged dumps it skipped. Module parameter a52_regdump: 1 (default) = this behaviour, 2 = every call as 5.4,
0 = changes only. Nothing else in the driver moves; the registers are still read every call (same I2C traffic).
Expected: the "sm5714-charger: regmap:" lines drop from ~64 to ~2-5 per minute at steady state (changes during
charging phases still print); about 8.5 of 9.2 KiB/min saved = 7 % of the awake One UI log volume (116 KiB/min).
The two dev_info "sm5714_chg_get_property: psp=N" / "wdt kick" lines per cycle are left alone (5.4 has them).

